  "_function_fallback_rule": "Same shape as function_rules, consulted only after every function_rules needle has missed on both title and description. This tier is for generic categories that name no specialisation: as an ordinary rule they would win the longest-needle contest and strip specialisations off postings ('software engineer' is 17 characters, 'backend' is 7), so they must not compete with the specialised rules at all. A fallback rule can only ever claim a posting that would otherwise be 'other'. Keep the needles specific to the category: a bare ' engineer ' here would sweep up the process, manufacturing, test and mechanical engineers that correctly sit in 'other'.",
