  "_city_alias": "The city picker and the ?city= filter read JobFacets.city, which enrich.py fills with the first usable segment of the ATS location string VERBATIM. Two employers therefore spell one city two ways (Bangalore / Bengaluru) and split its count. city_aliases folds a lowercased spelling onto the display name we show; the value is also what ?city= is matched by. Keep keys lowercased -- cities.py folds before lookup -- and comma-free: what reaches the fold is ONE segment of the location string, so a key spelling a comma form can never match (test_no_alias_key_contains_a_comma). Adding a key here is safe; it only ever merges counts.",
